@* Popover's Overview, written by hand after Button's and Menu's: a form in a popover previewed in
   each mode, placement and width, staying open, your own trigger, and opening it from the server
   or C# (code). Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A popover is a panel beside its trigger that the user can leave without choosing anything. It suits filters, a small form or an explanation.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>For a list of actions, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/menu">Menu</Anchor>. For a task that needs an answer, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/dialog">Dialog</Anchor>. For a short label on hover, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/tooltip">Tooltip</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A form in a popover</Heading>
<TextBlock>A popover can contain anything, such as a <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor> that filters the page. To give the panel a heading, set <Code>Title</Code>; it also names the panel for screen readers.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="popover-filters" />
<TextBlock>On a static page, submitting a form in the panel closes it, and it opens again if the form comes back with errors. On an interactive page, close it from the submit handler: bind <Code>@@bind-Open</Code> and set it to false.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Placement and width</Heading>
<TextBlock>A popover opens below its trigger, aligned to its start (<Code>BottomStart</Code>), by default. To open it on another side, set <Code>Placement</Code>. It's as wide as its content, up to 24rem; for a set width, set <Code>PanelWidth</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="popover-sides" />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>When there's no room on its side, the panel moves to the other side.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When a panel beside the trigger fits on neither side, it opens below the trigger.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>In browsers without CSS anchor positioning, <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor> places the panel. With JavaScript off in those browsers, it opens in the middle of the screen.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Staying open</Heading>
<TextBlock>To keep a popover open while the user works elsewhere on the page, set <Code>AutoClose="false"</Code>. Escape, a click outside and other popovers no longer close it, so it shows a close button.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="popover-manual" />
<TextBlock>To add the close button to an <Code>Auto</Code> popover, or remove it from a manual one, set <Code>ShowCloseButton</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A custom trigger</Heading>
<TextBlock>A popover can open from a button of your own, such as an info icon. Set <Code>Trigger</Code> to the button, and pass it <Code>context</Code> with <Code>@@attributes</Code>, which connects it to the panel.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="popover-info-button" />
<TextBlock>The trigger must be a <Code>button</Code> with a name of its own. Without <Code>Trigger</Code>, the built-in button requires a <Code>Label</Code>. To style the built-in button, set <Code>StartIcon</Code>, <Code>Accent</Code>, <Code>Variant</Code> and <Code>Size</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Opening from the server or C#</Heading>
<TextBlock>A popover can be open when the page loads; set <Code>Open</Code>. On interactive pages, to open and close it from C# and follow what the user does, bind it with <Code>@@bind-Open</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@FromCode</Code>
<TextBlock>A popover opened this way leaves focus where it is. <Code>Open</Code> from the server requires IzzyBlazor's script. With JavaScript off, the panel stays closed until the user presses its trigger.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The close button has a name for screen readers. To set it for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>CloseLabel</Code></td><td>The close button's name</td><td>"Close"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Popover Label="Filters" StartIcon="Lucide.ListFilter" Title="Filter issues">
            <Form Model="Filters" FormName="filters" OnValidSubmit="ApplyAsync">
                <Checkbox @bind-Value="Filters!.Mine" />
                <FormActions>
                    <Button Submit Size="ControlSize.Sm">Apply</Button>
                </FormActions>
            </Form>
        </Popover>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "filters")]
            private IssueFilters? Filters { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() => Filters ??= new();
        }
        """;

    private const string FromCode = """
        @* Interactive page: opens when C# sets _tipOpen, and follows the user. *@
        <Popover Label="What's new" Title="What's new" @bind-Open="_tipOpen">
            Saved filters are here: pick one from the list.
        </Popover>

        @code {
            private bool _tipOpen = true;
        }
        """;
}
